.TH SYS-GUARDIAN 1 "October 2026" "sys-guardian 3.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sys-guardian \- system-wide hardware & integrity guardian for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sys-guardian
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sys-guardian
is an ultra-lightweight system daemon and CLI utility designed to proactively monitor Linux system integrity, VFIO / GPU passthrough stability, thermal limits, storage block I/O, and active package manager locks.
.PP
Installed as a native system service in
.BR /etc/systemd/system/sys-guardian.service ,
it listens directly to kernel ring buffer events in real-time (<1s latency). When a critical hardware failure (such as a GPU falling off the PCI bus) or dangerous state occurs,
.B sys-guardian
issues an instant desktop alert to the active graphical session, generates an actionable diagnosis, stores the incident in a persistent 2-record Blackbox in
.BR /var/log/sys-guardian/ ,
and temporarily locks power actions (shutdown/reboot) using
.BR systemd-inhibit
to prevent filesystem corruption and kernel panics on shutdown.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Displays the current system integrity status (\fBNORMAL\fR or \fBBLOCKED\fR).
.TP
.B check
Performs an immediate one-shot scan across all sensors and logs.
.TP
.B diagnose
Outputs detailed triage information including GPU status, PCI drivers, QEMU VM process states, DPKG locks, thermal zone readings, and active power inhibitors.
.TP
.B simulate \fI[gpu|oom|io]\fR
Injects a simulated hardware failure into the kernel ring buffer to verify real-time alert and inhibitor triggers.
.TP
.B log-last
Displays the latest incident report stored in the persistent Blackbox (/var/log/sys-guardian/crash_latest.log).
.TP
.B log-prev
Displays the previous incident report stored in the Blackbox (/var/log/sys-guardian/crash_previous.log).
.TP
.B unblock
Removes the current shutdown/reboot lock and releases the systemd inhibitor.
.TP
.B test
Sends a test desktop notification to the currently active graphical session.
.TP
.B daemon
Starts the continuous real-time monitor listening to kernel events via journal inotify.
.TP
.B version
Displays version information.
.TP
.B help
Displays the command-line help screen.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/sys-guardian.service
Systemd system service unit.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/sys-guardian
Primary executable binary.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/sys-guardian-tray
Desktop StatusNotifierItem tray indicator applet.
.TP
.I /var/log/sys-guardian/crash_latest.log
Persistent report of the most recent critical incident.
.TP
.I /var/log/sys-guardian/crash_previous.log
Persistent report of the preceding critical incident.
.TP
.I /run/sys-guardian/sys-guardian.lock
Lock file generated when an integrity issue is detected.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
System is healthy, no active issues detected.
.TP
.B 1
An issue was detected or power actions are blocked.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR systemd-inhibit (1)
.SH AUTHOR
DriveMegaOrigin (https://github.com/DriveMegaOrigin/sys-guardian)
